      "title": "Handling Duplicate Tickets with Mixed Symptoms (Crash, Data Mismatch, Browser Issues)",
      "content_summary": "Guidance on closing duplicate tickets that contain inconsistent or contradictory symptom reports, such as application crashes alongside data mismatches.",
      "content_body": "When multiple tickets describe the same user issue but cite conflicting symptoms like browser inconsistencies and hard crashes, first verify if they are truly duplicates. Insufficient initial information often leads operators to create separate tickets for each perceived symptom rather than one comprehensive report. If the underlying case is identical, close the additional tickets as duplicates to maintain accurate reporting metrics. Ensure the primary ticket has been escalated to engineering or resolved via configuration changes before closing the secondary ones."
